          "narratives": {
            "headline": "WAF's 4QCY25 result delivered group production of 112koz in line with pre-released guidance, with a stronger-than-expected Kiaka ramp-up offsetting softer Sanbrado output and group AISC of A$2,401/oz beating forecasts by 6%, closing CY25 at 300koz and leaving WAF well-positioned for a material step-up to ~455koz in CY26.",
            "exec_summary": "West African Resources delivered a solid 4QCY25 result, with group gold production of 112koz \u2014 up 21% quarter-on-quarter \u2014 largely in line with pre-released guidance and analyst forecasts, capping a full-year CY25 tally of 300.3koz at the lower end of the company's guidance range. A stronger-than-expected performance from the Kiaka operation (62.3koz) offset a softer Sanbrado quarter (49.7koz), while group AISC of A$2,401/oz came in approximately 6% below prior estimates, reflecting the benefit of lower costs at Sanbrado (A$2,152/oz). The balance sheet ended the period in robust shape, with cash of A$584m and bullion on hand of A$177m \u2014 a combined liquid position that surged approximately 73% quarter-on-quarter \u2014 underscoring the company's rapidly strengthening financial position as Kiaka scales toward full capacity. Overall, the tone of the quarter is constructive: the Kiaka ramp-up is progressing well, recoveries have improved to 92.9%, and the operation is now connected to stable grid power, supporting confidence in the CY26 production outlook of approximately 455koz.",
            "production": "West African Resources delivered group production of 112koz in 4QCY25, up 21% quarter-on-quarter, with the result broadly in line with expectations following a pre-release. Kiaka was the standout performer, contributing 62.3koz on the back of better-than-expected head grades of 1.0g/t (versus the 0.9g/t estimate) and recoveries of 92.9%, demonstrating clear progress in the ramp-up trajectory. Sanbrado, meanwhile, came in below expectations at 49.7koz, though the shortfall was more than offset by Kiaka's outperformance, with the group closing CY25 at 300.3koz \u2014 at the lower end of guidance.",
            "outlook": "With Kiaka ramping toward an estimated 245koz contribution in CY26 and group production forecast at ~455koz, WAF is positioned for a material step-change in output and free cash flow generation, supported by a strong net cash and bullion position of A$761m exiting CY25. Key catalysts include continued Kiaka throughput and grade performance as the operation scales toward steady-state, while the primary risks remain cost inflation in Burkina Faso, sovereign and security risk in the Sahel region, and any deterioration in the prevailing gold price."
